APPENDIX: HOW THIRD-PARTY DEVELOPERS CAN APPLY CPOSLS-1.0 TO THEIR OWN PROJECTS
================================================================================
To license your own software, specification, or documentation under CPOSLS-1.0:
1. Place a copy of this file named `LICENSE` in the root of your repository.
2. Replace the Copyright, Project / Work, and URL lines at the top with your
   own name/organization, project name, and URL.
3. Optionally include the following short header in your source files:

   Copyright (c) YEAR <ORIGINAL AUTHOR NAME / ORGANIZATION>
   Licensed under the Calyx Public Open Source Specifications v1.0 License
   (CPOSLS-1.0). Completely FOSS — Original Author Attribution required.
